      <memberdef kind="typedef" id="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_shard_r_p_c_client_1a9115a696d3f1bb16ad0b55e05d10b784" prot="public" static="no">
        <type>std::function&lt; nlohmann::json(std::string, nlohmann::json)&gt;</type>
        <definition>using themis::sharding::ShardRPCClient::InProcessResponseHandler = 
std::function&lt;nlohmann::json(std::string ,
                             nlohmann::json )&gt;</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>InProcessResponseHandler</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::sharding::ShardRPCClient::InProcessResponseHandler</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Inject a custom response handler for the in-process simulation path. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>When set, <computeroutput>handler</computeroutput> is called by sendRequestInProcess() instead of the built-in hardcoded responses. This enables test and integration code to:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>simulate NACK/abort responses (&quot;vote&quot;: &quot;abort&quot;)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>inject network-timeout exceptions</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>exercise partial-failure and circuit-breaker code paths</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The handler receives the RPC method name (e.g. &quot;prepare&quot;, &quot;commit&quot;) and the full <computeroutput>params</computeroutput> JSON and must return a well-formed response JSON. Pass <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> to restore the built-in hardcoded fallback behaviour.</para>
<para>Thread safety: the handler is stored under the impl mutex; it is safe to call this method from any thread before or during RPC use.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>handler</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Callable matching <computeroutput>nlohmann::json(std::string, nlohmann::json)</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> to clear. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
